<title>SINGAPORE: National Kap first half loss deepens.</title>
<headline>National Kap first half loss deepens.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of S$ unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss		     (1.10)   vs   (0.70)</p>
<p>    Group shares (cents)     (5.76)   vs   (3.67)</p>
<p>    Turnover			8.12    vs    9.47</p>
<p>    Other income		  0.01    vs    0.02</p>
<p>    Interest on borrowing     0.35    vs    0.24</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation 0.69    vs    0.92</p>
<p>    Associates		    0.11    vs    0.03</p>
<p>    Tax			     0.05    vs    0.30   (gain)</p>
<p>    Minority			0.02    vs   (0.05)</p>
<p>Note - Electronics components maker National Kap Ltd said difficult conditions in the global electronics industry were expected to continue into the next year and it did not expect any improvement for the remainder of this year.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
